(7641213, 1240433, 77543, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> Darren .. i absolutely loved this in voting .. and am so glad you got in the top 5 .. <br/>its brilliant .. <br/>and i was interested to know the lens you used for this shot .. Canon EF 70-300mm f/4.0-5.6 IS USM .. can you be quite far away from the insects and zoom in .??. <br/>with the macro lenses i have used .. canon and olympus .. i have to be very close to the insect .. i''d love the ability to be a lot further away .. i dont think the mirrorless omd em1 Mk2 lenses have that ability .. :(<br/> <br/>and just realized the breakdown of votes and Sara''s comment .. very disappointing seeing those low votes .. as this really is exceptional .. :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you, Im pleased you liked the picture.<br/> <br/>I was about a metre away if I recall correctly. I think I had an extension tube on my lens. This is how Im able to get a fairly large magnification without getting too close.</td>', 'Originally posted by roz: Darren .. i absolutely loved this in voting .. and am so glad you got in the top 5 .. its brilliant .. and i was interested to know the lens you used for this shot .. Canon EF 70-300mm f/4.0-5.6 IS USM .. can you be quite far away from the insects and zoom in .??. with the macro lenses i have used .. canon and olympus .. i have to be very close to the insect .. i''d love the ability to be a lot further away .. i dont think the mirrorless omd em1 Mk2 lenses have that ability .. :( and just realized the breakdown of votes and Sara''s comment .. very disappointing seeing those low votes .. as this really is exceptional .. :)   Thank you, Im pleased you liked the picture. I was about a metre away if I recall correctly. I think I had an extension tube on my lens. This is how Im able to get a fairly large magnification without getting too close.', '2019-09-11 19:17:27.000000', NULL, 0),
